From: Horizon authors <>
Subject: [PATCH] Position the Continue view once after collision relocation

initializeDrawingOffsets adds a projection delta; it is not idempotent.
initializeLoadedMap calls it twice. The original queued pan eventually hid
the doubled offset, but removing that redundant pan exposes it: in Green Gym
the drawing origin stays at Y=384 instead of 242 and clips the tamer.

The USA NPC visibility loop marks present NPCs visible without projection,
so it does not need the preliminary adjustment. Position/upload the view once
at the existing final call, after any collision/story relocation. Preserve the
other regions' existing preliminary visibility path.
---
 src/main/main.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/main/main.c b/src/main/main.c
--- a/src/main/main.c
+++ b/src/main/main.c
@@ -3907,7 +3907,11 @@ void initializeLoadedMap(void)
 
 	STORED_TAMER_POS = TAMER_ENTITY.entity.posData->location = SAVED_STATE.playerPos;
 	PARTNER_ENTITY.digimonEntity.entity.posData->location = SAVED_STATE.partnerPos;
+#if !VERSION_IS(US)
+	/* USA marks NPCs visible below without projection. Its additive camera
+	 * adjustment belongs only at the final position, after relocation. */
 	initializeDrawingOffsets(MAP_TILE_DATA.tiles);
+#endif
 
 	for (i = 0; i < 8; i++) {
 #if VERSION_EQUAL_OR_OLDER(JP_BOMBOM)
